+
+## Creating a JSON Patch
+
+`createPatch(from, to)` returns a JSON Patch (RFC 6902) that turns `from` into `to` when applied; neither input is
+mutated. The patch only describes what changed: objects and arrays are compared recursively, an item added to or
+removed from an array is a single `add` or `remove`, and a moved item is removed and added back, without rewriting the
+items around it. Values of different kinds are replaced at their path (`""` for the whole document):
+
+```ts
+import { createPatch } from "./src/index.ts";
+
+createPatch({ a: [1, 2, 4], b: 1 }, { a: [1, 2, 3, 4], b: 1 }); // [{ op: "add", path: "/a/2", value: 3 }]
+```
