@@ -0,0 +1,14 @@
+## Context
+
+`applyPatch` already exists; `createPatch` is its inverse. Inputs are plain JSON values.
+
+## Decisions
+
+- Recursive diff: objects by key (own keys), arrays by alignment, otherwise `replace`. Differing kinds (object/array/scalar/null) replace the whole value.
+- Arrays: compute a longest common subsequence under deep equality. Items outside it are removed (descending index) and added (ascending index); where a gap holds both removed and added items they are paired positionally and diffed recursively, so an edited item is patched in place rather than removed and re-added. This gives single `add`/`remove` for insertions/deletions and remove+add for moves, never touching items in between. `move` ops are not emitted (permitted alternative).
+- Values placed in the patch are deep-cloned.
+- Operations are emitted so that each index is valid when applied sequentially.
+
+## Risks
+
+LCS is O(n·m) per array; acceptable for payload sizes. Trim common prefix/suffix first to keep typical cases cheap.
