@@ -0,0 +1,20 @@
+## Why
+
+Clients want to send only what changed between two versions of a JSON document. The library can apply a JSON Patch but cannot produce one.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Add `createPatch(from, to)`, exported from `src/index.ts`, returning an RFC 6902 patch that turns `from` into `to`.
+- The patch is minimal in spirit: it recurses into objects and arrays, and inserted, removed or moved array items do not cause neighbouring items to be rewritten.
+- Inputs are never mutated. README documents the function.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+- `json-patch`: adds patch generation alongside patch application.
+
+## Impact
+
+- `src/index.ts`, `src/index.test.ts`, `README.md`. No breaking changes.
